{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789796080,"nonce":"EprZ+YrR1T5HIFNTzGwmoQMtZXM=","title":"Python: KeyError carries a string, so a non-string key prints quoted","message":"`KeyError.__str__` returns `repr(self.message)`, right for a raised\n`KeyError(\"msg\")` (CPython: `'msg'`) and wrong for a library lookup that\nmissed, which stores `str(key)`: a tuple key prints as `'(8, 8)'` and an\nint key as `'5'` where CPython prints `(8, 8)` and `5`. The exception\nholds a `message: Str`, not the key object, so the two cases cannot be\ntold apart afterwards. Carrying the key (or its repr with a flag) needs\n`BaseException.message` to take an Object.\n\nAlso: `x in s` on a set of eight values or fewer scans without hashing,\nso an unhashable value (a list) tests False instead of raising TypeError\nas CPython does; the same holds for the shaped probes.","files":null}]}